जम्बाल जम्बाल, अस्, अम्, m. n. mud, clay;
an aquatic plant, Vallisneria; (अस्), m. a fragrant
plant, Pandanus Odoratissimus.

जम्बूल, अस्, m. the plant Pandanus Odoratissi-
mus; the plant Eugenia Jambolana [cf. जम्बू];
(अम्), n. jests addressed to the bridegroom by his
female relatives and friends; [cf. the following.]
—जम्बूल-मालिका, f. a garland of Jambūla flowers;
brightness of countenance in a bride and bridegroom;
jesting compliments addressed to the bride and bride-
groom by the female relatives of the bridegroom.

जामदग्न जामदग्न, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. जमद्-
अग्नि), derived from or produced by Jamad-agni;
(अस्), m., N. of a Catur-aha ceremony.
